 ## Background
-The method originates from implementations of isosurface ray casting, specifically demonstrated in the `isovolume-ray-casting` project [S1, unofficial]. It is based on the standard Lambertian reflectance model, which assumes that light is scattered equally in all directions from a surface [S1, unofficial]. The addition of shadow rays is a common technique in computer graphics to enhance realism [S1, unofficial]. The concept of using a single point light source for shading is also discussed in the context of OpenCL volume raycasting [S2, unofficial].
